#: manual/conventions.md:1
msgid "Repository conventions"
msgstr "リポジトリ規約"

#: manual/conventions.md:3
msgid "These rules add to the Luna-Flow documentation standard for `mooncake_impact_factor`. The repository combines a MoonBit score package, a Python index builder, and a Next.js application, so its documentation must keep all three in step."
msgstr "以下は、Luna-Flow のドキュメント標準に加えて `mooncake_impact_factor` が定めるルールです。このリポジトリは MoonBit のスコアパッケージ、Python のインデックスビルダー、Next.js アプリケーションから成るため、ドキュメントでは三者の整合を保つ必要があります。"

#: manual/conventions.md:8
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "範囲"

#: manual/conventions.md:10
msgid "Describe the current **`0.1.2`** baseline on the branch."
msgstr "ブランチ上の現在の **`0.1.2`** ベースラインを説明します。"

#: manual/conventions.md:11
msgid "Do not document unpublished commands, routes, fields, or MoonBit exports."
msgstr "未公開のコマンド、ルート、フィールド、MoonBit のエクスポートは記述しません。"

#: manual/conventions.md:12
msgid "When behavior is local-only, say so directly instead of implying a global service contract."
msgstr "ローカル限定の挙動は、グローバルなサービス契約があるかのように書かず、その旨を明記します。"

#: manual/conventions.md:15
msgid "Consistency"
msgstr "整合性"

#: manual/conventions.md:17
msgid "`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and the manual must tell the same release story."
msgstr "`README.md`、`CONTRIBUTING.md`、マニュアルは同じリリースの経緯を説明しなければなりません。"

#: manual/conventions.md:18
msgid "API docs must match the actual MoonBit package name, function signatures, and Next.js route contracts."
msgstr "API ドキュメントは、実際の MoonBit パッケージ名、関数シグネチャ、Next.js のルート契約と一致しなければなりません。"

#: manual/conventions.md:19
msgid "If Python scripts expose stable CLI flags, database behavior, or search semantics, document them explicitly."
msgstr "Python スクリプトが安定した CLI フラグ、データベースの挙動、検索セマンティクスを公開する場合は、それを明示的に記述します。"

#: manual/conventions.md:20
msgid "Distinguish local registry facts from authoritative mooncakes facts."
msgstr "ローカルレジストリ上の事実と、mooncakes が権威を持つ事実を区別します。"

#: manual/conventions.md:21
msgid "If Python and MoonBit intentionally share the score formula, keep both docs and code paths aligned."
msgstr "Python と MoonBit が意図的にスコア式を共有する場合は、両方のドキュメントとコードパスを揃えます。"

#: manual/design/score.md:1
msgid "Score Design"
msgstr "score 設計"

#: manual/design/score.md:3
msgid "The current scoring model combines four signals:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:5
msgid "total package dependents"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:6
msgid "recent dependents inside the rolling 180-day activity window"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:7
msgid "optional download snapshot volume"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:8
msgid "release recency multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:10
msgid "Why These Inputs Exist"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:12
msgid "Total dependents capture established ecosystem adoption."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:13
msgid "Recent dependents reward active new integration, not only historical weight."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:14
msgid "Download counts provide an external popularity hint when available."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:15
msgid "Release recency reduces stale-package bias without making age the primary ranking factor."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:17
msgid "Current Formula"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:27
msgid "The logarithms intentionally compress very large packages so the ranking does not become a pure dependent-count leaderboard."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:30
msgid "Current Release Multipliers"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:32
msgid "`<= 30` days: `1.12`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:33
msgid "`<= 90` days: `1.06`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:34
msgid "`<= 180` days: `1.00`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:35
msgid "`<= 365` days: `0.94`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:36
msgid "`> 365` days: `0.88`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:38
msgid "Rank And Momentum Layers"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:40
msgid "Rank labels are coarse score buckets:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:48
msgid "Momentum labels use score-delta rules exported from MoonBit and are materialized by the Python index builder:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:51
msgid "`Rising`: growth `>= 35`, ratio `>= 0.35`, recent dependents `>= 3`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:52
msgid "`Hot`: growth `>= 18`, ratio `>= 0.18`, recent dependents `>= 2`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:53
msgid "`Stable`: otherwise"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:55
msgid "The build pipeline persists momentum labels for serving, while MoonBit remains the source of truth for the rule definitions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:58
msgid "Data Flow"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:60
msgid "`scripts/build_index.py` reads local `*.index` records from the MoonBit registry snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:61
msgid "The builder reconstructs packages, versions, dependencies, package edges, and the FTS search index in SQLite."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:62
msgid "The Python pipeline calls the local MoonBit CLI to compute score snapshots, rank labels, activity multipliers, and momentum labels."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:63
msgid "`src/score` exposes the score, rank, momentum, and snapshot logic for MoonBit consumers and local CLI reuse."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:64
msgid "`lib/query.ts` defines the shared query AST, native-expression parser, serializer, and compatibility helpers used by both server and client."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:65
msgid "The Next.js app reads the generated SQLite database and serves feeds, search results, advanced query building, and package analysis views."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:67
msgid "Implementation Constraint"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/score.md:69
msgid "The repository intentionally keeps Python responsible for database generation and SQLite materialization, while MoonBit owns the reusable score, rank, momentum, and snapshot rules that the local CLI forwards into the build flow."
msgstr ""

